[WORK]
UID: WORK-GRAMMAR-FILE-SPLIT
TITLE: Split the grammar into spec, plan and annotations files
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
Split the one grammar into multiple .sgra files grouping functionality,
with cross-grammar relations. The operator's proposed divide, explicitly
not settled: spec.sgra holds the definition family (MECHANISM, DECISION,
EVIDENCE, REQUIREMENT) and probably coverage (USE_CASE); plan.sgra
holds WORK, though they could hear an argument to merge it with spec;
review/annotations.sgra holds the annotation class (WORK-ANNOTATION-NODES).

The multi-grammar assumption is UNVERIFIED. The operator
assumed strictdoc allows it because its online docs bake grammars
directly into .sdoc documents, and names that an assumption, not a
measurement. A spike is agreed as needed and precedes any cut: two
grammar files, one relation whose two ends import different grammar
files -- does strictdoc resolve it. The session-5 two-grammar sketch
(packages/strictdoc-grammar/values/{plan,spec}.nix, wired to nothing)
recorded the same assumption as UNVERIFIED. Note for grooming:
DEC-ONE-GRAMMAR (accepted) currently rules ONE grammar; acting on this
item means superseding it, which is the operator's call, not this node's.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Ambiguity the operator flagged themselves -- USE_CASE's home: "coverage: use
case? I think it slots here as a form of contract but could also be seen as
work (test coverage)."

Operator, 2026-09-01, verbatim: "sounds like a spike is needed. i assumed
yes as they bake grammars directly into sdocs in their online docs. that's
why i assumed yes. but it is an assumption."
